{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You’ve been admitted because of a gastrointestinal bleed. Can you tell me about your symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, doc. I’ve had blood in my stool for about four days now. Not black or tarry, just mixed in. I’ve been feeling weak, dizzy, and really tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you had dialysis the day before coming in. Your hematocrit dropped from 33.9 to 22.6, which is significant. We gave you one unit of blood in the ER. How’s your breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little short, especially when I lie down. I started coughing yesterday too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows some fluid in the lungs—moderate pulmonary edema. Given your heart and kidney history, this is likely from fluid overload. We’ll monitor that closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I feel so puffy? My legs are okay, but I just feel heavy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s consistent. We’ll adjust your medications and plan for dialysis tomorrow to help remove excess fluid. But first, we need to find the source of the bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had bleeds before—stomach and intestines. But not since I stopped blood thinners."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. You’re not on Coumadin due to past bleeds. We’ll avoid anything that could worsen bleeding. We’re starting you on IV fluids and a proton pump inhibitor to reduce stomach acid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been itching like crazy since I got here. Is that from the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have prurigo nodularis, which we see in some dialysis patients. We’ll continue your Aquaphor, Sarna, and Benadryl as needed. It’s not from new meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. What’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do an upper endoscopy tomorrow to look for the bleed source. You’ll be sedated, and we’ll check your esophagus, stomach, and duodenum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be awake?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2149-09-06 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be asleep during the procedure. You’ll wake up shortly after. It’s very safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2149-09-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re getting you ready for your endoscopy. Any questions before we go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2149-09-07 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’m ready. Just want to know what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. The endoscopy showed severe esophagitis—significant inflammation in your esophagus. That’s likely where the bleeding came from. There was also mild duodenitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Esophagitis? Like acid reflux?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You also have a small hiatal hernia, which can make reflux worse. We’re switching you to high-dose IV pantoprazole to help it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on omeprazole. Is this stronger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re giving it twice daily. You’ll go home on 40 mg twice a day. Also, no NSAIDs—no ibuprofen, naproxen, or aspirin except your 81 mg heart dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my heart rate? It’s been racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "After the procedure, you were in rapid atrial fibrillation. We gave IV diltiazem and increased your oral dose to 60 mg four times a day. It’s under control now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on diltiazem already. Is that safe with my heart failure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We restarted it cautiously. It helps control your rate. We held your usual long-acting dose initially but are now on a short-acting form you take four times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2149-09-07 13:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding lisinopril for now due to the bleed and low hemoglobin. Diltiazem will help with both rate and pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2149-09-07 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had two more units of blood. How’s my count now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2149-09-07 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had three total. Your hemoglobin is stabilizing. We’ll check it again tomorrow. You’re not actively bleeding now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2149-09-07 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What about dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2149-09-07 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have hemodialysis this afternoon. It will help clear fluid and toxins. We’ll monitor your heart during it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs show your potassium dropped to 3.0 and magnesium to 1.9. You had two brief episodes of NSVT—non-sustained ventricular tachycardia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? I felt a flutter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but we caught it early. We’ve given potassium and magnesium supplements. No further episodes since. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. My belly’s been hurting—left side."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray. No perforation or obstruction. There’s some increased lung opacities on the left, likely from the edema. Pain may be from that or bowel irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No colonoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2149-09-08 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not now. Since the upper endoscopy found a likely source and you’re not bleeding now, we’ll do outpatient colonoscopy and repeat EGD in a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your CMV and HSV antibodies. CMV IgG is positive, IgM negative—means past exposure, not active infection. HSV IgG positive, but no signs of outbreak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this time. CMV can reactivate if immunity drops, but you’re stable. No treatment needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My graft site hurts. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. The renal team thinks it could be steal syndrome. They recommend seeing transplant surgery as an outpatient to evaluate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Am I getting better overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2149-09-09 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your breathing is better, no active bleeding, heart rhythm stable. We’re planning discharge tomorrow if all stays well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your labs are stable. We’re discharging you today. You’ll go home on high-dose omeprazole, continue all other meds except lisinopril for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your PCP, GI for repeat endoscopy and colonoscopy, and transplant surgery for your graft pain. Get a CBC drawn next week and fax it to your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my weight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Weigh daily. Call if you gain more than three pounds in a day. That could mean fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2149-09-10 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and keep up with your appointments."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
